# Debug DB onboarding convention

Keep debug resource growth predictable, strictly typed, and consistent in `/debug`.

## Goal

Add a new debug-inspectable DB resource with minimal edits while preserving strict validation and stable UX.

## Source of truth

- `services/domain/db/debug/registry.ts` composes resource metadata.
- Resource slices live in:
  - `services/domain/db/debug/resources/singletons.ts`
  - `services/domain/db/debug/resources/collections.ts`
  - `services/domain/db/debug/resources/endpoints.ts`
- Runtime loading is centralized in `services/domain/db/debug/load-debug-resource.ts`.

## Required checklist

1. Add query in `services/domain/db/queries/<group>/<kebab>/<kebab>.ts` plus fields in `services/domain/db/queries/<group>/<kebab>/<kebab>.fields.ts` (endpoints may omit `.fields.ts`).
2. Add repository in `services/domain/db/repositories/<group>/<kebab>.ts`.
3. Register metadata in `services/domain/db/debug/resources/<group>.ts` with:
   - `kind` (`"singleton" | "collections" | "endpoints"`)
   - `key` (stable technical key used in debug URLs)
   - `label` (display fallback)
   - `labelKey` (i18n key under `debug.resources.*`)
4. Wire server loader in `DEBUG_RESOURCE_LOADERS` within `services/domain/db/debug/load-debug-resource.ts`. Collections also need `DEBUG_COLLECTION_COUNT_LOADERS` (React `cache()` around the count repo).
5. If kind/labels are visible in UI, add i18n keys in `i18n/debug/es.json` (`debug.kind.*`, `debug.resources.*`) and `i18n/db/es.json` (`db.<key>.failed_to_fetch`; collections also `not_found`).
6. Keep validation strict: invalid `kind` + `resource` must resolve to `null`.

## Existing examples

- Singleton: `site_settings`, `header`, `footer`, `whatsapp_button`, `services_button`
- Collection: `pages` (and the rest of Schema collections)
- Endpoint: `health`

## Guardrails

- Do not reintroduce manual switch-based resource dispatch.
- Do not duplicate manual resource lists outside the `registry.ts` -> `catalog.ts` flow.
- Keep `catalog.ts` derived from `registry.ts`.
- Keep TypeScript strict (`no any`, `no @ts-ignore`).
- Keep invalid `kind`/`resource` paths null-safe and crash-free.
- Collections load one page only (`page` default 1, `limit` default 10, never `limit: -1`, never dump-all).
